{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/410357-scenario-idea-werewolf-meets-parasite-eve","id":410357,"title":"Scenario Idea: Werewolf meets Parasite Eve","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-18T11:26:54-08:00","id":410357,"title":"Scenario Idea: Werewolf meets Parasite Eve","content":"Sans zombies. Because they're overdone and not much of a threat to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Concept</u></b><br /> Werewolves forced into a closed, subterranean environment full of warped, twisted, shapechanging monstrosities. By itself, not a huge departure from a lot of games. But it's an excuse to pop the claws and have some gory fun.<br /> <br /> And that's not all!<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mr. Johnson</u></b><br /> The way I'm currently imagining it, this wouldn't be the first scenario. For full fun, it requires a pre-existing, antagonistic relationship with a Mad Science, Inc. Cheiron Group, Last Dynasty International, Pentex, whatever. They were working on some sort of bioweapon or cure or <i>thing</i>, and it got out of hand in a secret facility near enough to the PC's territory. Eventually the Mad Science Inc. (MSI) brass gets desperate enough to call in a favor with the PCs.<br /> <br /> So the party gets a call from a former enemy, asking for help. After the uproarious laughter dies out, the contact manages to convince the party (perhaps with a show of good faith, maybe with an offer of money or a cease-fire, whatever you think is best) that &quot;No, for real guys, we're serious&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Plan</u></b><br /> The Pack gets briefed. There's a huge underground complex literally crawling with the twisted spawn of Clive Barker and John Carpenter's nightmares, and the humans are at their wits' ends. They can't send in human or mortal assets because they get infected by a super-aggressive, evil parasite and almost immediately start to mutate. Even teams loaded up with guns in biohazard suits don't last long because suddenly those monsters started growing claws that could shred through the biohazard gear.<br /> <br /> See, the PCs are being called in because werewolves are known to be immune to disease. While they still will have to be careful of the creepy claws and such, they have at least a chance of making it.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the Storyteller should also make sure that the research lab's Shadow is full of terrifying spirit-things as well. Twisted forms born out of the cold, awful experiments performed here. The Court of Unhindered Progress it is called. They'll strap a werewolf's spirit-form down to a freezing dissection table and slice it open to pull out &quot;interesting&quot; components.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Problems Arise</u></b><br /> Immune or not, though, MSI gives the party an ultimatum: &quot;We're not letting anything out of that lab once it goes in. Try to come back out and you'll find fire and silver waiting for you. You might be immune, but you could still be a carrier.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's where the questions arise. Do you split up the party? How will you extract the assault team? Do you even risk it? Especially after MSI says, &quot;You are our last option before we go nuclear.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><u>Feedback</u></b><br /> And there you have it. I think this could be a very compelling game, but I'm wary of this sort of &quot;low option, high risk&quot; adventure. Failure could mean that the player who goes in dies, sure, but worse failure could mean that the entire chronicle is brought to a violent, hot, nuclear halt. Granted, it could make for an interesting story regardless, and as the cap to a Chronicle could be very cool win or lose.<br /> <br /> How might you go about handling such a game? Both in-character and as a player/Storyteller.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:09:32-08:00","id":410418,"title":"","content":"So in other words, a City Urban Wyrm Game where the Garou are in a desperate end of the world kind of thing. I use both Parasite Eve games I own to help me flesh out ideas on Wyrm creatures.<br /> <br /> This looks fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:17:07-08:00","id":410425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/410357-scenario-idea-werewolf-meets-parasite-eve?p=410418#post410418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, a City Urban Wyrm Game where the Garou are in a desperate end of the world kind of thing. I use both Parasite Eve games I own to help me flesh out ideas on Wyrm creatures.<br /> <br /> This looks fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...er...hmm.<br /> <br /> Never having played Apocalypse, but understanding surface elements (Wyrm, Wyrm taint, Pentex, etc...), I'm surprised it took until now for me to see the similarities. I mean, I wasn't assuming that this was a totally unique idea, just an interesting one.<br /> <br /> But yeah, wow, now that you say it this totally fits Apocalypse. I guess the question is &quot;How to make this more Forsaken-y?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or not, could be a fun diversion from a more Forsaken-y game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:36:44-08:00","id":410504,"title":"","content":"I never played the game, but I saw the movie, which based on your description sounds completely different.<br /> <br /> However you could have your science team 'awaken' the mitochondrial shards in the Human host, who then awaken others as they come into contact in an attempt to reform the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitochondrial_Eve\" target=\"_blank\">First</a>.<br /> <br /> But that would be a bit much for me. You could take advantage of the weirdness of virus spirits, which appropriately don't find it into any known classification of spirit as detailed in the Book of Spirits. Those spirits could be altered and then ride or claim the infected into becoming more efficient virus-delivery mechanisms. I'm sure there's something like the Thing from John Carpenter in the Predators book. Or you could use the idigam. <br /> <br /> The advantage of having an intelligence behind the problem is that captured or downed werewolves don't have to be killed. The creator of whatever is infecting people may be curious enough about the werewolves and their immunity to have them brought back alive. That would be one of the changes I'd go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:45:46-08:00","id":410507,"title":"","content":"Actually I have never played <i>Parasite Eve</i>, or seen the movie, or read any of the books. I just know that it has John Carpenter-esque monsters in it, and I was watching a Let's Play of the first few minutes of the first game when I came up with the idea (wonder how that happened).<br /> <br /> Having an intelligence behind it would also give the assault team a real target and objective beyond &quot;Kill everything in the base&quot;, so that sounds like a good change. I hadn't considered the idigam angle before, but that could work. Assuming that the players didn't catastrophically screw things up (the aforementioned nuclear option), it could lead into a larger investigation that reveals the idigam behind it all.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure Cheiron/LDI/whatever would <i>love</i> to confront whoever's messing with their experiments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:59:28-08:00","id":410518,"title":"","content":"Not sure if mentioned already, but the Idigam can make some freaky shit. Hunting ground the Rockies has a su'ur that is an uratha (essentially) merged with an azlu. It's not to far a stretch. You could get 20th book of the wyrm for some nifty inspirations, and just make it an idigam of corruption. I keep kicking around an idea to make weaver, wyld and wyrm all idigam that are in fierce opposition. Mostly because I love the black spiral tribe and to just convert them to bake hounds seems a waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}